From 5e6f708192a3b4c5d6e7f8091a2b3c4d5e6f7081 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude Fable 5.1" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 8 Sep 2026 06:10:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 9/10] mmc: sdhci: the 1.8 V signalling bit is not SD-only

SDHCI_CTRL_VDD_180 in Host Control2 describes the level the host drives the
bus at. It is a property of the wiring, not of the card type: an eMMC whose
VCCQ rail is 1.8 V needs it set exactly as an SD card in UHS-I does, and eMMC
HS200 and HS400 are defined only at 1.8 V.

sdhci_set_voltage() nevertheless writes the bit only for SD, in both the 3.3 V
and the 1.8 V arm, so an eMMC is always driven at 3.3 V no matter what
mmc->signal_voltage says. The regulator handling right above is already
card-type agnostic, which is the giveaway: the supply gets switched and the
controller does not follow it.

On hardware the result is a bus that enumerates and then cannot move data --
CMD is one line and tolerant enough to survive the wrong level, the eight data
lines are not.

Drop the two IS_SD() conditionals so the bit follows mmc->signal_voltage. For
SD nothing changes; for eMMC the host now matches the supply.

Signed-off-by: open-nanokvm-pro contributors <nanokvm@localhost>
---
 drivers/mmc/sdhci.c | 24 ++++++++++--------------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/sdhci.c b/drivers/mmc/sdhci.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/sdhci.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/sdhci.c
@@ -577,22 +577,17 @@
 				}
 			}
 #endif
-			if (IS_SD(mmc)) {
-				ctrl &= ~SDHCI_CTRL_VDD_180;
-				sdhci_writew(host, ctrl, SDHCI_HOST_CONTROL2);
-			}
+			ctrl &= ~SDHCI_CTRL_VDD_180;
+			sdhci_writew(host, ctrl, SDHCI_HOST_CONTROL2);
 
 			/* Wait for 5ms */
 			mdelay(5);
 
 			/* 3.3V regulator output should be stable within 5 ms */
-			if (IS_SD(mmc)) {
-				if (ctrl & SDHCI_CTRL_VDD_180) {
-					pr_err("3.3V regulator output did not become stable\n");
-					return;
-				}
+			if (ctrl & SDHCI_CTRL_VDD_180) {
+				pr_err("3.3V regulator output did not become stable\n");
+				return;
 			}
-
 			break;
 		case MMC_SIGNAL_VOLTAGE_180:
 #if CONFIG_IS_ENABLED(DM_REGULATOR)
@@ -613,22 +608,17 @@
 				}
 			}
 #endif
-			if (IS_SD(mmc)) {
-				ctrl |= SDHCI_CTRL_VDD_180;
-				sdhci_writew(host, ctrl, SDHCI_HOST_CONTROL2);
-			}
+			ctrl |= SDHCI_CTRL_VDD_180;
+			sdhci_writew(host, ctrl, SDHCI_HOST_CONTROL2);
 
 			/* Wait for 5 ms */
 			mdelay(5);
 
 			/* 1.8V regulator output has to be stable within 5 ms */
-			if (IS_SD(mmc)) {
-				if (!(ctrl & SDHCI_CTRL_VDD_180)) {
-					pr_err("1.8V regulator output did not become stable\n");
-					return;
-				}
+			if (!(ctrl & SDHCI_CTRL_VDD_180)) {
+				pr_err("1.8V regulator output did not become stable\n");
+				return;
 			}
-
 			break;
 		default:
 			/* No signal voltage switch required */
-- 
